-- C5-INTEL roadmap rows (2026-11-05, charter pillars autonomy, cost, reach; request "code, deploy and close all open roadmap and backlog tasks", cluster C5-AUTONOMY).
-- Rows 6, 8, 129 and 132 of roadmap_implementation carried status text written on 2026-09-30 and 2026-10-06. Each is re-read below against live qnfo-audit and main, and set to what is true;
-- none is closed to lower a count, and each names its open remainder with an owner and a probe.
--   6   RM-S4-BENCHMARK-1            not-built -> partial   CODE-BATTERY-1 built and deployed (PR 7416, qnfo-code-orchestrator 0.47.0); the first run is in progress, so verification is pending.
--   8   RM-NOVEL-FAILURE-REPAIR-1    partial   -> partial   the mechanism the row asks for is live as BREACH-DOCTOR-1 (breach_playbooks + doctor); what is left is authoring playbooks for the gap families.
--   129 RM-TP-4-COST-FLEET-40        partial   -> partial   levers 1 to 7 stated with their live state; the exit (a $40 fleet run rate) is far from met and the owner ceiling is now USD 200-300 all-in.
--   132 RM-TP-7-REACH-REVIEW-GATE    partial   -> partial   levers 1 and 2 are done and live, 3 is the c5-observe row, 4 is conditional, 5 is owner-held; the exit metrics are outcomes; one conversion experiment is filed.
-- APPLY-BY: ci
-- DB: qnfo-audit
-- BACKUP: bak_20261105_c5_intel_rows
-- Rollback: UPDATE roadmap_implementation SET status = (SELECT b.status FROM bak_20261105_c5_intel_rows b WHERE b.id = roadmap_implementation.id), evidence = (SELECT b.evidence FROM bak_20261105_c5_intel_rows b WHERE b.id = roadmap_implementation.id), verified_at = (SELECT b.verified_at FROM bak_20261105_c5_intel_rows b WHERE b.id = roadmap_implementation.id), artifact_ref = (SELECT b.artifact_ref FROM bak_20261105_c5_intel_rows b WHERE b.id = roadmap_implementation.id) WHERE id IN (6, 8, 129, 132) AND EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM bak_20261105_c5_intel_rows b WHERE b.id = roadmap_implementation.id); -- the issue row below stays (close it with evidence instead of deleting)
-- NOOP-OK: the guarded UPDATEs match only the status each row had when it was read; a replay matches nothing and the issue insert is guarded by its title.

CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS bak_20261105_c5_intel_rows AS
SELECT id, status, evidence, verified_at, artifact_ref
FROM roadmap_implementation
WHERE id IN (6, 8, 129, 132);

-- ---- 6: RM-S4-BENCHMARK-1 --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
UPDATE roadmap_implementation
SET status = 'partial',
    artifact_ref = 'qnfo-code-orchestrator',
    evidence = evidence || ' | 2026-11-05 c5-intel: CODE-BATTERY-1 built and deployed, verification pending. PR 7416 merged 2026-11-05T00:33:37Z, qnfo-code-orchestrator /health reads 0.47.0-codeagent at 00:37Z, ops_config code_battery_state shows run cb-1-2026-11-05 started 00:34:45Z with 52 pairs (13 tasks x 4 ladder models, one pair per minute-tick). The battery is 13 SWE-bench-style and Terminal-Bench-style tasks graded by running the model code against hidden tests in a Dynamic Worker (no network, CPU limit); results go to benchmark_results (task_id cb-1:*), report_card_inputs coding_battery_pass_rate and coding_battery_detail, and the metrics coding_battery_pass_rate and coding_battery_age_days (guard, trigger at over 9 days). It is a labelled PROXY of those suites (13 tasks, no repositories, no containers), not SWE-bench Pro or Terminal-Bench. The artifact moved from qnfo-ai-calibration (no LOADER binding there and the canonical deploy installer does not install worker_loaders) to qnfo-code-orchestrator (LOADER, AI binding, ladder options). Before it, the only model benchmark was arc_agi_10task_pass_rate 0.2 from 2026-09-10 and 8 ops tasks from 2026-09-19. Verify: SELECT key, value, updated_at FROM report_card_inputs WHERE key LIKE ''coding_battery%''; SELECT model, COUNT(*) n, SUM(pass) ok FROM benchmark_results WHERE task_id LIKE ''cb-1:%'' GROUP BY model. Remainder: cb-2 with harder tasks when a rate of 0.95 or more repeats (validity finding); a reviewed change to feed the SAI thinking dimension from it (the formula is untouched here).'
WHERE id = 6
  AND item = 'RM-S4-BENCHMARK-1'
  AND status = 'not-built';

-- ---- 8: RM-NOVEL-FAILURE-REPAIR-1 --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
UPDATE roadmap_implementation
SET verified_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now'),
    evidence = evidence || ' | 2026-11-05 c5-intel (live reads 2026-11-04 22:40Z to 23:00Z): the mechanism this row asks for, a failure-class to repair library with automatic dispatch and verification, is live as BREACH-DOCTOR-1 (docs/breach-doctor/README.md; engine block in qnfo-fleet-control, every 10-minute tick plus the qnfo-cloud-ops second runner). Library: breach_playbooks holds 26 rules over 13 families (24 mode on, 2 measure), each with trigger_sql, action_sql, revert_sql and verify_sql. Dispatch: ops_config breach_doctor = on, v_breach_doctor_status shows 185 cases in 24 h. Verification: a case is verified only after two passes of its verify_sql, 11 verified and 0 failed in 24 h, doctor_actions_failed_24h = 0, doctor_tick_age_min = 11. The older remediation_modules table (8 probe lanes for scripts/remediation_consumer.py) is the first-generation form and stays as the consumer lane list. What is NOT covered is the novel classes: v_breach_doctor_status.unclassified_cases = 326 in 22 gap families (other 148, METRIC-TRIGGER 63, OWNER-REQUEST 29, LOOP-BREAKER-1 25, CODE-LOOP-EXHAUSTED-1 9, METRIC-REGRESSION-1 8, CHAOS-DRILL-FAILED-1 6, ...). A sample of the 148 in other shows a long tail of one-off titles, the 63 METRIC-TRIGGER cases are open metric breaches and breach_code_task_pct reads 100.0, so a breach whose lever is code already reaches the code loop, and the rest need a class-specific closing test; a playbook that only relabelled them would lower the count without repairing anything, so none was added here. The gap is graded and routed: metrics breaches_undiagnosed_over_60m (313, target 0) and breaches_auto_remediated_24h (11, target 12 or more) each have an enabled trigger whose lever is a playbook row by migration for the largest unclassified family; umbrella issue 1000266 is open; the playbook-gap rule (family-level gap issues) is deliberately in measure mode (control breach-doctor-gap-measure) because a gap issue has no code-task a doer can edit. Remainder: authoring the next playbooks from the triggers above, one family at a time.'
WHERE id = 8
  AND item = 'RM-NOVEL-FAILURE-REPAIR-1'
  AND status = 'partial';

-- ---- 129: RM-TP-4-COST-FLEET-40 ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
UPDATE roadmap_implementation
SET verified_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now'),
    evidence = evidence || ' | 2026-11-05 c5-intel (live reads 2026-11-04 to 2026-11-05): the exit is far from met and the target moved. Account meter (cost_daily workers_ai): 2026-11-02 USD 40.34, 11-03 39.03, 11-04 31.95 (2.91 M neurons); metrics fleet_ai_run_rate_30d_usd 542.99 (counters, which understate the meter 2.4x to 2.9x), workers_ai_cost_30d_usd 514.04, monthly_cost_run_rate_usd 1248.54 (7-day run rate x 30 including USD 450 owner-stated direct providers), ns_fleet_cost_usd_month 859.38 (2026-11-05T00:37Z) against the owner ceiling USD 200-300 all-in set 2026-11-04. The USD 40 of this row is the stretch target; the ceiling the fleet is graded on is ns_fleet_cost_usd_month <= 300. Lever state: (1) separate lines: cost_usd_30d excludes owner-local spend (USD 227.89) and v_cost_all_in splits meter, estimate and owner-stated; session_ai_spend_30d_usd and owner_client_spend_30d_usd are not registered metrics. (2) prefix cache: PROMPT-CACHE-1 (PR 691, 7 workers), PROMPT-CACHE-CODE-1 (6950), PREFIX-CACHE-AGENTS-1 (7136) merged; ai_spend_ledger cached_tok 10.15 M of 40.6 M input tokens for qnfo-agents on 11-04 (25 percent for the whole day, 88 percent in the 11-minute window PR 7136 measured); ai_cache_hit_rate 0.06 against a target of 0.3. (3) draft-verify ladder: RM-COST-L6-DRAFT-VERIFY-1 is still partial. (4) one prober: PROBER-FOLD-1 folded the health prober into qnfo-ai-calibration; the 5-minute meter shows the pings at about 8 neurons each, not a cost line. (5) cheaper-model switches: COST-CUT-CODE-1 (PR 7247, glm before kimi, dear-rung output caps), PR 6921 (gpt-oss first rung), TWIN-FLASH-1. (6) governors: code_loop_daily_neurons 100000 (PR 6982), q08 (7000), research tick allowance (7060), QNFO-AGENTS-BUDGET-1 (7187, qnfo_agents_daily_neurons 250000, 1.04 M to about 0.27 M neurons a day expected), AGENTS-LEAN-1 (7213) and AGENTS-INPUT-CUT-1 (7273); v_spend_enforcement is expected to show its first clean day on 2026-11-05 (not yet read). (7) reconciliation: cost_attribution_gap_pct 0 reads the ledger only; v_ai_meter_vs_counters (PR 7032) is the meter-side check and on 2026-11-04 it shows deepseek-v4.1-flash-1017 1.13 M neurons with 0 counted (qnfo-agents, before the 7187 governor), kimi-k2.6 364 k of 483 k unattributed (a burst in the :05 to :10 five-minute slots of each hour, 15 to 25 calls, 6 k to 13 k neurons an hour on 11-04; AI Gateway logs for 19:17Z to 23:17Z hold the pings, about 50 input tokens each with metadata worker qnfo-ai, and ten unlabelled calls of 6.7 k to 9.5 k input tokens, a minority of the burst, so most of it is direct binding calls, caller not yet named), gpt-oss-120b 111 k unattributed. workers_ai_attribution_coverage_pct reads 76.5 (2026-11-05T00:05Z). The ledger price bug (gateway @cf models priced at the GPT-5.5 rate) is fixed in code (PR 6985, 5.45.2) but 11-02 and 11-03 ledger rows still carry it. Remainder, each with a doer: issue 1001705 (COST-D1-DRILL-1b, calls the ledger does not see; closing probe = v_ai_meter_vs_counters attributed_pct for the top models), the 11-05 reading of the 7187 governor (v_spend_enforcement), and the draft-verify row 13. No new cost lever was shipped from this row: the one candidate that remains unowned is naming the :05 kimi-k2.6 caller, which needs a cron-by-cron read of the 5-minute meter, and it is recorded on 1001705.'
WHERE id = 129
  AND item = 'RM-TP-4-COST-FLEET-40'
  AND status = 'partial';

-- ---- 132: RM-TP-7-REACH-REVIEW-GATE ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
UPDATE roadmap_implementation
SET verified_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now'),
    evidence = evidence || ' | 2026-11-05 c5-intel (live reads 2026-11-04): lever 1, a subscribe box on every public page, is done: RM-SUBSCRIBE-CTA-1 (row 23) is built, and a live fetch of papers.qnfo.org/papers/<slug> shows the double opt-in form (section sub, form ld-sub-form posting to /api/subscribe) after the text; subscribe_funnel box_view over 30 days is papers 5574 (904 more classed bot), papers.qnfo.org reach-layer 516, qnfo.org 504, about 29. Lever 2, citation_pdf_url, is done: the meta tag is on a live paper page and scholar_pdf_backlog = 0 (written by qnfo-pdf every 10 minutes). Lever 3, the funnel monitor, is row 22 (prd_funnel_monitor_stale = 0). Lever 4, the monthly note, replaces the weekly digest only at 10 or more subscribers and there is 1 (3 pending, one of them the self-test). Lever 5 is owner-held and recorded (human_actions 1, 5, 6, 175 and 190 resolved or dismissed). The exit metrics are outcomes, not buildable: subscribers_growth_monthly = 0 (target text: owner-outcome, not autonomically closable) and credibility_events_90d is UNMEASURED by design since NOZ-DOI-1 (2026-10-10: the selected works DOIs no longer resolve, PERF_SELECTED_DOIS is empty until third-party-resolvable identifiers exist). The measured gap is conversion: 0 human submissions from about 6600 box renders in 30 days (1 self-test submit, 15 honeypot hits), subscribe_confirm_rate_30d 0.0, while engaged external readers are about 44 a week (engaged_reader_sessions_7d), so even a perfect box yields a handful a month. Filed as the next slice: ROADMAP-1 QNFO.REACH T7.1 (paper pages show the box only after the full text; a one-line above-the-fold link as a decision-rule experiment, code-task on qnfo-gateway lpSubscribe, probe marker PAPER-CTA-TOP-1). Remainder: that experiment, the readers (READER-YIELD-1 rows), and the owner-held identifiers.'
WHERE id = 132
  AND item = 'RM-TP-7-REACH-REVIEW-GATE'
  AND status = 'partial';

-- ---- the next slice of row 132, with a doer and a probe -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
INSERT INTO agent_issues (title, description, source, category, priority, status, created_at, updated_at)
SELECT 'ROADMAP-1: QNFO.REACH T7.1: paper pages show the subscribe box only after the full text; try an above-the-fold link with a decision rule',
 'code-task: repo=qnfo-workers path=qnfo-gateway/worker.js' || char(10) ||
 'code-anchor: function lpSubscribe(source) {' || char(10) ||
 'code-probe: {"paths": ["qnfo-gateway/worker.js"], "contains": "PAPER-CTA-TOP-1"}' || char(10) || char(10) ||
 'Charter pillar reach (program QNFO.REACH; roadmap row RM-TP-7-REACH-REVIEW-GATE, lever 1 follow-up). Metrics it should move: subscribe_submits_30d (1 on 2026-11-05, the self-test) and subscribers_growth_monthly (0, target +10 a month). Expected yield is LOW and this is an experiment with a decision rule, not a fix.' || char(10) ||
 'Evidence (subscribe_funnel, 2026-10-05 to 2026-11-04): box_view papers 5574, papers.qnfo.org reach-layer 516, qnfo.org 504, about 29 (904 more classed bot); stage submit: 0 from people (1 self-test), submit_honeypot 15; subscribe_confirm_rate_30d 0.0. A live paper page (papers.qnfo.org/papers/<slug>) holds its only subscribe form after the whole text, at about 74 percent of the HTML (section sub, form ld-sub-form). External engaged readers are about 44 a week (engaged_reader_sessions_7d, READER-YIELD-1), so the box is seen by few people who reach the end.' || char(10) ||
 'EDIT: in the paper page renderer (the function that calls lpSubscribe), add under the title or abstract one line of text, "Get the next paper by email", that links to the existing form (an id on the section) and sends one beacon on click to /api/funnel/view?source=paper-top-click (funnelViewSource already accepts that name, so no new endpoint and no new table). No second form, no pop-up, no change to the double opt-in or to the copy of the existing box. Name the change PAPER-CTA-TOP-1 in a comment, bump qnfo-gateway with scripts/worker_release.py, add a test that the line is on a paper page and that the beacon source is accepted.' || char(10) ||
 'Decision rule (recorded in decision_log by the doer): keep if, over 28 days, subscribe_funnel source paper-top-click holds at least 20 clicks and subscribers rows with source papers or paper-top-click grow by at least 1; otherwise remove the line (revert = delete it). Failure mode: the extra link changes nothing because the readers who reach a paper are bots or the owner; then the lever is readers, not the box (READER-YIELD-1).' || char(10) ||
 'Definition of done: merged and verified live by the canonical deploy (a fetch of a live paper page shows the line and the marker is in the code); after 28 days the decision above is written to decision_log with the two numbers. The gateway file may be claimed by another session at the time of filing: take the work claim before editing.',
 'session:c5-intel', 'feature', 'medium', 'open', CAST(strftime('%s', 'now') AS INTEGER) * 1000, CAST(strftime('%s', 'now') AS INTEGER) * 1000
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM agent_issues WHERE title = 'ROADMAP-1: QNFO.REACH T7.1: paper pages show the subscribe box only after the full text; try an above-the-fold link with a decision rule');
